# 8. Kubernetes RBAC

RBAC means:

**Role-Based Access Control**

It controls permissions inside Kubernetes.

Architecture:

```text
User

↓

Role

↓

RoleBinding

↓

Permission
```

---

# 9. RBAC Components

Main objects:

* Role
* ClusterRole
* RoleBinding
* ClusterRoleBinding

---

# 10. Role

A Role defines permissions inside a namespace.

Example:

Allow viewing Pods:

```yaml
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1

kind: Role

metadata:

 name: pod-reader


rules:

- apiGroups: [""]

  resources: ["pods"]

  verbs: ["get","list"]
```

---

# 11. RoleBinding

Connects a user with a Role.

Example:

```text
User

↓

RoleBinding

↓

Role

↓

Permission
```

---

Example:

```yaml
kind: RoleBinding

metadata:

 name: read-pods


subjects:

- kind: User

  name: developer


roleRef:

 kind: Role

 name: pod-reader
```

---

# 12. ClusterRole

ClusterRole works across the entire cluster.

Example:

Administrator permissions:

```text
ClusterRole

↓

All Namespaces

↓

All Resources
```

---

# 13. ClusterRoleBinding

Connects users to ClusterRoles.

Example:

```text
Admin User

↓

ClusterRoleBinding

↓

Cluster Administrator
```

