# 15. Service Accounts

A Service Account provides identity to Pods.

Example:

```text
Pod

↓

Service Account

↓

Permissions
```

---

Create:

```bash
kubectl create serviceaccount app-sa
```

---

Use in Pod:

```yaml
spec:

 serviceAccountName: app-sa
```

---

# 16. IAM Roles for Service Accounts (IRSA)

IRSA connects Kubernetes Service Accounts with AWS IAM Roles.

Without IRSA:

```text
Application

↓

AWS Access Keys

↓

S3
```

Problem:

* Credentials inside application
* Security risk

---

With IRSA:

```text
Application Pod

↓

Kubernetes Service Account

↓

IAM Role

↓

AWS Service
```

---

# 17. IRSA Example

Application:

```text
Backend API Pod
```

Needs:

```text
Amazon S3 Access
```

Flow:

```text
Pod

↓

Service Account

↓

IAM Role

↓

S3 Bucket
```

No AWS keys required.

